          deckDescription: 'A standard 32-tile Chinese domino set used for Ce Deng and related games. The set has 21 unique tiles plus 11 duplicates: two of each of the 11 civil tiles (all doubles 1-6 and [3:1], [6:5], [6:4], [6:1], [5:1]) and one each of the other 10 military tiles; there are no blanks.',
          suitDescription: 'Chinese domino tiles do not use Western suits; each tile has two ends with values from 1 to 6 (often named: 6 Dragon, 5 Plum, 4 Blood, 3 Slant, 2 Two, 1 Nail). The 32-tile set divides into civil (duplicated) and military (single) tiles.',
          rankDescription: 'Each end of a Chinese domino tile shows a value from 1 to 6, represented with pip patterns similar to dice. Tiles are described by their two ends, e.g. [5:3]. Doubles are called stubborn and are harder to play.',
